2026-09-23: TODO T01 historical issue reconciliation, not a new campaign.

Authority and populations
-------------------------
The September 15 application-ledger construct table is historical. This record
joins its identities to checked-in regressions and later original results.
It does not assert that all language features, all non-PASS programs, or the
entire TODO are done. There are no message-only E3101/FP waivers in this join.

Torture before: .evidence/ladder/e0/20260914T154648Z/results.jsonl
  SHA256 eded7dfc18473d4d26b2a9e3c4480c74e688a2def95b192de5db867927a8ebb0
Torture after: .evidence/ladder/e0/20260919T222317Z/results.jsonl
  SHA256 70eb261de86b81db5ea1e60f5b89e5eef0b832300fba8c1b6ff43d62db81b85f
Both contain the same 1692-program population. The 114 old E3101 rows include
107 compiler-failures, six already FP-deferred, one already not-applicable.
The 107 previously unclassified failures map to 88 PASS, 15 named deferrals
(14 binary128 -> L02; one floating-vector -> L05), and four evidenced
not-applicable cases. All 114 map to 92 PASS / 17 FP-deferred / 5 not-applicable.
Every row was rechecked with existing e0.classify_program against the actual
source, current review's SHA256 and evidence files. Historical PASS means the
cited complete run, not execution again with today's compiler.

LLVM old identities: .build/vector-targeted/llvm-e3101-targeted.jsonl
  SHA256 bfbc2092d6c7bbe91a807bf87ffa19b06eb14adbe4fb8f75fd912bef20a9bef9
All 148 source hashes still match the pinned checkout. Complete later results:
  .evidence/ladder/llvm-test-suite/20260919T230110Z/results.jsonl
  SHA256 a038af1819d0f71ac20321103ab1247d24b8d57df400326b458bae70d74f0b6a
They map to 119 PASS / 16 compiler-failure / 10 FP-deferred / 2 not-applicable /
one oracle-unusable. Every one of the 16 failures is in the separately
reconciled 44-row B01 table, tests/fixtures/llvm-failure-reconciliation.out:
three later targeted PASS (lu, ludcmp, 20020720-1), 12 named FP deferrals,
one OPEN timeout (floyd-warshall -> B02). No arithmetic promotion of old totals.
The two not-applicable rows are F01 zero-parameter arity (20051012-1) and
the original unsupported -ffast-math option (pr39501), not unknown FP.
gramschmidt retains its failed original reference control; not a subject PASS.

Construct -> regression -> original -> remaining boundary
--------------------------------------------------------
Paths in this section are under tests/fixtures unless specified.

Inline asm:
  assembly-general-update.c, assembly-tied-width.c,
  assembly-tied-pointer-width.c; language_semantics.rs constraint tests.
  pr65053-1, pr65053-2, pr65956, pr88904, 20030222-1 all PASS in the
  cited torture run. Constraint-specific rules remain; this is not an
  assertion that every architectural asm dialect is supported.

Calls/declarations:
  legacy-integer-declarations.c, unprototyped-function-pointers.c and
  prototype-array-members.c; external_symbol_lowering.rs and parser tests.
  F01 keeps 920501-1, 921202-1, 921208-2 not-applicable: zero-parameter
  definitions are called with arguments. legacy-discarded-return.c keeps
  920728-1 not-applicable: Clang rejects its non-void bare return even GNU89.
  GNU/ISO inline declaration chains: inline_definition_roles.rs; actual
  FORTIFY/SCSI object replays are in the existing kernel ledger, not emitter
  suppression. No validator is weakened.

VLA:
  variable-array-cast.c, variable-array-cast-entry.c,
  variable-array-label-scopes.c, variable-array-alloca-lifetime.c,
  variable-array-ended-lifetime.c, variable-array-typeof-profile.c.
  20040811-1, 20221006-1, 920721-2, 920929-1, pr43220, vla-dealloc-1
  and c-testsuite 00207 PASS in the later original runs.
  variable-array-original-refusals.out names all 12 oracle-rejected original
  extensions (four nested-function, eight record VLA-member cases).
  Pointer-to-VLA typeof evaluation disagreement remains L08, not all VLA.

Static addresses / representation:
  relative-label-table.c passes same-function table dispatch; language_semantics
  retains the negative for narrowing then widening a label difference (E3026).
  20030216-1, 20031214-1, pr70460 PASS. Floating object representation is not
  automatically FP execution; later scalar FP support supersedes only the
  specific former scalar refusals, not long double/FP vectors.

Aggregate varargs:
  mixed-record-varargs.c, mixed-record-varargs-driver.c,
  mixed-record-varargs-worker.c, integer-complex-varargs.c;
  language-semantics.out and integer-complex-varargs.out.
  c-testsuite 00140, torture 920625-1/pr44575 PASS in later full runs.
  HFA/HVA oracle limitations are B04; sub-eight-byte external vector ABI is
  L06. A failing reference self-control is never a compiler PASS.

Pointer qualifications:
  null-conditional-qualification.c and array-pointer-qualification.c/.out;
  source element qualifiers, bounds and nested-pointer negative tests remain.
  c-testsuite 00144's raw later run passes, but its uninitialized condition
  is not the semantic oracle; the defined-condition reduction is the check.
  Landlock fs.o/net.o assemble with matching two/two exports each.

Atomics, frames and integer complex:
  atomic-read-modify-write.c, ancestor-return-address.c,
  integer-complex-values.c plus integer-complex-varargs.c (see language-semantics.out).
  pr122000 and 20041124-1 PASS. 20010122-1/20030323-1 are source-bound
  oracle-conflict dispositions, not ancestor-frame support; L09 remains.
  Integer-complex division remains L07. Additional atomic boundaries are
  inventoried in atomic-scope-boundaries.c/.out and tracked in L11a-L11c.

E3101:
  The complete joins below retain every historical identity. The two E3101
  diagnostics in the entire later torture run are 920728-1 (above) and
  991014-1 (extreme-array layout, independently evidenced oracle conflict);
  neither is waived as floating point.
  The newer independent always-inline failures have explicit regressions:
  inline-value-transport.c and inline-complex-parameter.c, repaired in
  21ffded and measured in private-leaf-substitution.out (T01a).

Current targeted health check, not original campaign rerun:
  CARGO_TARGET_DIR=target/frontend CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true cargo test -p evocc
    --test language_semantics --test private_leaf_substitution --offline -j 2
  63 + 5 PASS, zero FAIL/ignored, release subject unchanged.
  .build/floating-targeted/atomic-scope-20260923/reconciliation-gate.log
Full application, kernel and compiler acceptance remain B10/K13/K14/T04/T05.

